-- title:
--   Locally height-normalised full level structures coincide
-- statement:
--   The statement is a uniqueness assertion for full level-$n$ structures on a fake elliptic curve over a Noetherian base, under a hypothesis of being a height-normalised level transport after every base change to a connected base. Its hypotheses fall into the following groups.
--
--   **Numerical data.** Primes $r$ and $\bar r$ with $\bar r \neq r$, and a non-zero natural number $N$ which is squarefree and divisible by neither $r$ nor $\bar r$.
--
--   **Coefficients.** A characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$ which is a discrete valuation ring, an irreducible element $\pi$, completeness of $\mathcal O$ for the $(\pi)$-adic topology, $\#(\mathcal O/\pi)=r$, and $(r)=(\pi)$ in $\mathcal O$; a characteristic-zero field $K_0$ which is a fraction field of $\mathcal O$. Further, an $\mathcal O$-algebra $Onr$ which is a characteristic-zero domain, an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $Fr$ of $Onr$, completeness of $Onr$ for the ideal generated by $\pi$, maximality of that ideal, the condition `hOnr_alg` that every element of $Onr$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$, the condition `hOnr_closed` that every monic polynomial over $Onr$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$, and `hFr`: $Fr(x)\equiv x^{r} \pmod{\pi}$ for all $x$. Finally a homomorphism $vdet\colon \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to \mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) characterised by `hvdet`: $vdet(g)=n$ if and only if $\det g = u\,\pi^{n}$ for some $u\in\mathcal O^\times$.
--
--   **The indefinite quaternion algebra and its moduli.** Rationals $a,b$ with `hB`: $0<a$ or $0<b$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathbb Z$ the completion $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ is a division algebra exactly when $v$ contains $r$ or $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda$. A scheme $\mathcal X$ with a morphism $f$ to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, an assignment $pt$ of points to fake elliptic curves with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ structure, and `h𝒳` asserting that this is a coarse moduli datum (invariance under isomorphism, compatibility with base change, bijectivity on algebraically closed fields, and the universal property). A level $n\ge 3$ with $r\nmid n$, $\bar r\nmid n$ and $\gcd(n,N)=1$; a scheme $M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with point assignment $ptF$ for curves with full level $n$ and `hM` the fine moduli property; a group $G$ with $\rho\colon G\to\operatorname{Aut}M$ and labels $\chi\colon G\to\Lambda$ satisfying `hρ`, the level-twisting action property. A morphism $p\colon M\to\mathcal X$ with $p$ followed by $f$ equal to $f_M$, invariant under $\rho$, and compatible with the two point assignments (`hp_pt`). For each prime $\ell\notin\{r,\bar r\}$, a coarse moduli datum $(\mathcal Y_\ell,g_\ell,ptT_\ell)$ for curves with extra level $\ell$, together with degeneracy morphisms $d_0,d_1\colon\mathcal Y_\ell\to\mathcal X$ over $\mathcal O$ whose effect on moduli points is forgetting the extra level (`hd₀`), resp. passing to an $\ell$-isogeny quotient (`hd₁`). Morphisms $a_r,a_{\bar r}\colon\mathcal X\to\mathcal X$ over $\mathcal O$ realising on points the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $r$ and at $\bar r$.
--
--   **The definite quaternion algebra and its arithmetic groups.** Rationals $a_1,b_1$ with `hdef`: $a_1<0$, $b_1<0$ and $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ division at exactly those height-one primes containing $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda_1$, an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ with $R_1\le\Lambda_1$, a finite idele $n_1$ in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $r$ such that the intersection order $R_1\cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ is Eichler of level $Nr$; an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra map $\iota_0\colon\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]\to M_2(K_0)$; a height-one prime $v$ containing $r$. A subgroup $\Gamma_t$ of units, identified by `hΓt` with the units integral away from $v$ for $R_1$; elements $s_\ell$ and ideles $sf_\ell$ indexed by primes $\ell\notin\{r,\bar r\}$ satisfying the four clauses of `hs` (agreement of $sf_\ell$ with $s_\ell$ at all places away from $r$, triviality at $r$, membership of the diagonal idele of $\ell$ times $sf_\ell^{-1}$ in the level Hecke set of the intersection order when $\ell\mid N$ and in its prime Hecke set otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell)=\ell$); the groups $\Gamma_{t,\ell}=\Gamma_t\cap s_\ell\Gamma_ts_\ell^{-1}$; and a unit $\bar w$ of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\Gamma_t$.
--
--   **Coordinates on the order.** The hypothesis that every rational integer lies in $\Lambda$, and a map $coord\colon\Lambda\to \mathbb{W}(\mathbb F_{r^2})\times\mathbb{W}(\mathbb F_{r^2})$ satisfying `IsOrderCoord`: additivity, $1\mapsto(1,0)$, the Frobenius-twisted multiplication rule, injectivity, $r$-adic density, and the trace condition.
--
--   **The special-fibre uniformisation package over $\overline{Onr}=Onr/\pi Onr$.** A fake elliptic curve $A_0$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ of height $4$, formal coordinates $\theta_0$ of degree $2$ along the unit section of $A_0$ with `hA₀` making $A_0$ a formal module via $coord$, $X_0$, $\theta_0$; families $e,e'\colon\Gamma_t\to\operatorname{End}(A_0)$ with $e\gamma$ over the base and degrees $\deg$. The hypotheses `hE1`, `hE1mul`, `hE1sc`, `hE1'`, `hE2`, `hE3`, `hE4` and `hE5a`–`hE5e` (summarised here) assert: each $e\gamma,e'\gamma$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$ preserving the level structure; multiplicativity of $\gamma\mapsto e\gamma$ up to powers of $r$ and the correct behaviour on rational scalars, together with the converse recognition of scalars; for every injective ring map of the centraliser of the $X_0$-action into $M_2(K_0)$, the existence of a matrix $g$ and of endomorphisms $\varepsilon$ of the formal group inducing $e\gamma$ on $\theta_0$ with image $r^{k_\gamma}g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$; the existence of $\Lambda$-labels for the action of $\Gamma_t$ on any full level-$n$ structure of $A_0$, with the cocycle and scalar congruences modulo $n$; the fact that over any algebraically closed field every $r$-power-degree level-preserving isogeny of a pullback of $A_0$ comes from some $\gamma\in\Gamma_t$ up to powers of $r$; and the existence of an order $R_2\le R_1$ with $r$-power denominators carrying a compatible action $\hat e$ on $A_0$ (additive, commuting with $\Lambda$, level-preserving, multiplicative, with the integral and reduced-norm relations, compatible with $e$ on $\Gamma_t$, and jointly realised by matrices as above).
--
--   **The Drinfeld-side package.** A ring map $\iota\colon \mathbb{W}(\mathbb F_{r^2})\to Onr$; a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\Phi$ over $Onr/r$ which is special for the reduction of $\iota$ and of height $4$; a moduli package $MD$ over $Onr$ which is a Zariski sheaf; a map $\eta$ sending rigidified objects to points of $MD$, with `hη` (three clauses: equality of $\eta$-values of admissible objects is equivalence of the rigidified objects, compatibility with base change, and local liftability of every point of $MD$ to an admissible rigidified object on a Zariski cover); an injective ring map $E_0$ of the centraliser of the $\Phi$-action into $M_2(K_0)$, with `hE₀`'s clause that its image consists, after scaling by a fixed power of $r$, exactly of matrices over $\mathcal O$. Next, a family of maps $eD$ from the points of the functor $G(\mathcal O,MD)$ to the product of the functor corepresented by $Onr$ with the Deligne-datum functor $\Omega(K_0,\pi)$, with the hypotheses `hnatD` (naturality in the base), `hbijD` (bijectivity), `hfstD` (the first component is the structural leg), `hGLD` (the $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$-action on $G$-points corresponds to the twisted action on pairs, consisting of the $-vdet$-Frobenius twist on the leg and pullback of the Deligne datum), `hPiD` (a $\pi$-translation twists the leg by $Fr$ and leaves the datum unchanged), and `hPiexD` (existence of $\pi$-translates). Also a ring map $\kappa$ factoring the reduction map of $Onr$ modulo $r$ through the reduction modulo $\pi$, a natural number $n_0$, and a series $\beta_0$ which is an isogeny of height $4n_0$ from $\Phi$ to the base change of $X_0$ along $\kappa$.
--
--   **Base point and Atkin–Lehner datum at $\bar r$ on the special fibre.** A full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$; a fake elliptic curve $A_{0w}$ over $\overline{Onr}$ with morphisms $aw,aw'$ exhibiting it as an Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ of $A_0$ (`hALw`), morphisms $bw,bw'$ forming an isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_w}$ from $A_{0w}$ to $A_0$ which preserves the level, and `hJOINTw`, asserting that the matrix realisation of the $\Gamma_t$-action can be chosen so that in addition the composite of $aw$ followed by $bw$ is realised by an endomorphism whose image under $E_0$ is $r^{k_w'}g\,\iota_0(\bar w)\,g^{-1}$.
--
--   **The parametrisation $\Xi$.** An assignment $\Xi$ sending, for each Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent and each $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi\colon Onr\to B$, a rigidified curve (a fake elliptic curve $E$ over $B$ together with a rigidification relative to $A_0$: curves $E_b$, $A_b$ over $B/\pi$ pulled back from $E$ and from $A_0$ along the residue leg, and a level-preserving isogeny pair of degree $r^{d}$ between them) to a point of the $G$-functor of $MD$, subject to `hΞleg` (over a connected $B$ the resulting leg is a Frobenius twist of $\psi$), `hΞnat` (compatibility with base change of rigidified curves), `hΞiso` (invariance under isomorphisms of rigidified curves compatible with the rigidification up to powers of $r$), and `hΞdef` (over a connected $B$ with $r$ nilpotent, and given a formal module structure $(X,\theta)$ on the curve via $coord$, an explicit description of $\Xi$ by a rigidified object $t$ with $t.X=X$, a twist index $j\le1$, the rig-transport relation for $\theta_0,\kappa,\beta_0$, admissibility of $t$ for $\iota$ and the $(-j)$-fold Frobenius twist of $\psi$, and $\Xi$ given by $\eta$ applied to $t$).
--
--   **The comparison hypotheses at $g_0$.** A matrix $g_0\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ together with: `heqΓ`, stating that over a connected base a translation of the rigidification by $e\gamma$ corresponds, for some $c\in\mathbb Z$, to the action of $r^{c}\,g_0\iota_0(\gamma)g_0^{-1}$ on $\Xi$-points; `heqW`, the analogous statement for an Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ (when $\bar r$ is invertible in $B$) and the element $\bar w$; `hK1`–`hK4` (summarised here), asserting that the $\Xi$-points whose leg is the $g_0$-twist of $\psi$ and which are related by the $g_0^{-1}$-twisted action to a given Deligne datum exist, are unique up to an isomorphism of rigidified curves, are compatible with base change along $\mathcal O$-algebra maps, and lift along surjections with square-zero-type kernels; `hC0e`, the existence over a connected Noetherian base, for any curve with a rigidification along the $g_0$-twisted leg and any formal module structure via $coord$, of a full level-$n$ structure which is a height-normalised transport of $P_0$ in the sense of `IsNormLevelTransport` (there is a section $Q$ of $A_b$ over $B/\pi$ lying over the reduction of $P_0$ through the residue leg, a formal module structure $(X,\theta)$ on the curve via $coord$, a twist index $j\le 1$ and an admissible rigidified object $t$ with $t.X=X$ and the rig-transport relation, such that the reduction modulo $\pi$ of the $r^{t.n}$-multiple of the level section equals $Q$ followed by $\varphi'$ and then by $g_b$); and `hC0u`, the corresponding uniqueness over any such base: two full level-$n$ structures which are both height-normalised transports along the same rigidification have the same underlying section.
--
--   **The data of the conclusion.** Let $B$ be a Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra in which $\pi$ is nilpotent, $\psi\colon Onr\to B$ an $\mathcal O$-algebra map, $E$ a fake elliptic curve over $B$ with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ structure, and $\varrho$ a rigidification of $E$ relative to $A_0$ along the leg obtained from $\psi$ by twisting with $Fr^{-vdet(g_0)}$. Let $P_n$ and $P_n'$ be full level-$n$ structures on $E$, and assume the two hypotheses $h$ and $h'$, which have the same shape: for every Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B_c$ with $\pi$ nilpotent in which every idempotent is $0$ or $1$, every $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\varphi_c\colon B\to B_c$, every fake elliptic curve $E_c$ over $B_c$ and morphism $g_c$ exhibiting $E_c$ as the pullback of $E$ along $\varphi_c$, every rigidification $\varrho_c$ of $E_c$ along the composite of $\varphi_c$ with the twisted leg which pulls $\varrho$ back, every full level-$n$ structure $P_c$ on $E_c$ whose section followed by $g_c$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}\varphi_c$ followed by the section of $P_n$ (for $h$), respectively of $P_n'$ (for $h'$), and every formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_c$ over $B_c$ with formal coordinates $\theta_c$ making $E_c$ a formal module via $coord$: the structure $P_c$ is a height-normalised transport of $P_0$ along $\varrho_c$ in the sense of `IsNormLevelTransport` for $Fr,\theta_0,\kappa,\beta_0,\Phi,\iota,coord$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** The underlying sections of the two full level-$n$ structures agree: $P_n.P = P_n'.P$ as morphisms $\operatorname{Spec}B\to E$ over the identity of $\operatorname{Spec}B$.
--
--   This is the uniqueness half of the construction of the height-normalised level-$n$ structure attached to a rigidified fake elliptic curve in the Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison: it upgrades uniqueness over connected bases to uniqueness over an arbitrary Noetherian $\pi$-nilpotent base, the comparison being required only after base change to connected bases. It is used in the construction of the equivariant Čerednik–Drinfeld families of points on the fine moduli scheme and in the tower of extra-level moduli schemes, and in the local lifting of such families along square-zero extensions.
